<article class="env-lemma" id="04G1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04G1">Lemma <span data-tag="04G1">67.38.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then $f$ is G-unramified if and only if $f$ is unramified and locally of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider any diagram as in Lemma <a href="/tag/03MJ" data-tag="03MJ">67.22.1</a>. Then all we are saying is that the morphism $h$ is G-unramified if and only if it is unramified and locally of finite presentation. This is clear from Morphisms, Definition <a href="/tag/02G4" data-tag="02G4">29.36.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>